# Experiment D: query load at four concurrency levels (1, 4, 8, 16; see load-tests/README.md).
# DRAFT. Unapproved and unexecuted. Valid only for scripts/run-experiment.sh --dry-run.
# Format: scripts/README.md, "Experiment manifest contract". No spaces in values.
# PLACEHOLDERS the human replaces before an approval record is written
# (the record binds the sha256 of the final file, so any edit needs a new record):
#   ACCOUNT_ID       123456789012 is the documented example, not a real account.
#   DATASET_SNAPSHOT a draft name; the dataset-engineer has not defined snapshot ids.
#   OUTPUT_ROOT      /abs/outside/repo/... is a placeholder path; pick a durable directory
#                    outside the repository.
# OPEN ITEM FOR THE HUMAN: the course text names 1, 10, 50 and 100 concurrent clients.
# The provisional tier caps (16 on M, 32 on L) make 50 and 100 unreachable, so the top
# level here is 16 (the tier M cap). No cap was raised.
# MAX_TASKS 3500 = 100 warm-up + 200 + 600 + 1000 + 1600 requests over the four levels.
# Cost basis: HOURLY_BURN_USD 0.85 = tier M session 0.62 + 2 extra runtime tasks 0.025
# + 4 load-test client tasks at 0.0494 (0.1975) = 0.8425, rounded up (UNVERIFIED rates).
# 0.85 x 90 min / 60 = 1.275. Uses the offline LLM stub, so no Bedrock charge.
MANIFEST_VERSION=1
EXPERIMENT_ID=D
DESCRIPTION=query-load-four-concurrency-levels-1-4-8-16-tier-m-draft
ENVIRONMENT=course
REGION=us-east-1
ACCOUNT_ID=123456789012
DATASET_SNAPSHOT=scholarchain-slice-m-25000-works-DRAFT
SIZE_TIER=M
MAX_MINUTES=90
MAX_CONCURRENCY=16
MAX_TASKS=3500
SPEND_CEILING_USD=1.50
HOURLY_BURN_USD=0.85
STOP_CONDITIONS=wall-clock,first-failure,spend-estimate
METRIC_NAMES=CPUUtilization,MemoryUtilization,DesiredTaskCount,RunningTaskCount,ThrottledRequests,SuccessfulRequestLatency,ReadThrottleEvents,MainRequestQueuePendingRequests
METRIC_NAMESPACES=AWS/ECS,ECS/ContainerInsights,AWS/DynamoDB,AWS/Neptune
OUTPUT_ROOT=/abs/outside/repo/scholarchain-experiments
ENTRY_POINT=script:load-tests/d-query-load/run.sh
